From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 06:11:48 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: a menu toggle starts inline terminals minimized
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Zeo next proposal §6.17 (ask 37). A long run of tool calls fills the
conversation's scroll with expanded terminal cards. Upstream already has
the setting, agent.expand_terminal_card (default true), applied when a
terminal card is created; it was reachable only by editing settings.json.

The agent menu gains a "Conversation" section with "Terminals Minimized
by Default". The toggle owns no setting of its own: minimized is
expand_terminal_card seen from the other side, written through
update_settings_file like the Agent Questions entries. A terminal
already on screen keeps the state it has; the setting reaches terminals
created after the change.

The read and the write live in terminals_minimized.rs, so they can be
tested without opening the menu, which exposes no entries to a test.
Tests: terminals_minimized::tests (the write inverts the upstream key;
the toggle reads it, checked after a user-settings update). They were
written with the code and not seen failing first; the helper is two
lines, and the menu wiring is proven by the Xvfb proof instead.
---

